<title>USA: Advanced Polymer Retin-A gel gets FDA OK.</title>
<headline>Advanced Polymer Retin-A gel gets FDA OK.</headline>
<dateline>REDWOOD CITY, Calif. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advanced Polymer Systems Inc said Monday the Food and Drug Administration had given it marketing clearance for Retin-A Micro microsphere 0.1 percent, a gel, for the treatment of acne.</p>
<p>The product has been licensed to Johnson &amp; Johnson's Ortho Dermatological unit, which will pay Advanced Polymer a $3 million milestone payment, the company said.</p>
<p>Advanced Polymer said that upon commercialization, which is expected in the current quarter, it will begin to receive royalties from Ortho on product sales.</p>
</text>
